; casterdefault.eval - a Caster with NO spell, as a file can hold one (code-review
; C99). Judged by tools/EditorTest.py phase 23, which first takes the spells
; casterload.eval read back OUT of its scratch world's files (the skeleton at 12,6
; in eval_arena.ent, the skel_coward kind in monsters.cat) and runs this as a new
; process: the load warns for both (the control for casterload's "no warning"),
; each dialog OPENS on no spell yet holds and shows the first one offered, and
; Esc puts the spell-less original back, so a reopen opens on none again.

logecho on
reset
timescale 0
echo --- inspector ---
editor inspect 12 6
editor inspector
editor inspector esc
editor inspect 12 6
editor inspector
editor inspector esc
echo --- dialog ---
monsterdialog skel_coward
monsterdialog esc
monsterdialog skel_coward
monsterdialog esc
echo --- end ---
